[agent:result]     Schedule the execution of the job.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     If a schedule for this job already exists, the method updates it.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     ```python
[agent:result]     # Defaults (None, None): HOPS_START_TIME = last execution time (= previous cron fire),
[agent:result]     # HOPS_END_TIME = current cron fire. Works on any cron — no per-schedule tuning needed.
[agent:result]     job.schedule(
[agent:result]         cron_expression="0 0 * ? * * *",
[agent:result]         start_time=datetime.now(tz=timezone.utc),
[agent:result]     )
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     # Fixed 2-hour window ending at the cron fire (e.g. 08:00 → 10:00 at 10:00):
[agent:result]     job.schedule(
[agent:result]         cron_expression="0 0 * ? * * *",
[agent:result]         start_time_offset_seconds=-2 * 3600,   # HOPS_START_TIME = fire - 2h
[agent:result]         end_time_offset_seconds=0,             # HOPS_END_TIME   = fire
[agent:result]         catchup=True,              # replay all missed intervals on recovery
[agent:result]         max_active_runs=2,         # allow at most 2 concurrent runs
[agent:result]     )
[agent:result]     ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Parameters:
[agent:result]         cron_expression: The quartz cron expression.
[agent:result]         start_time:
[agent:result]             The schedule start time in UTC. If `None`, the current time is used.
[agent:result]             Can be in the past.
[agent:result]         end_time:
[agent:result]             The schedule end time in UTC. If `None`, runs indefinitely. Can be in the past.
[agent:result]         catchup:
[agent:result]             If True and the scheduler missed fires (outage, etc.), create one execution per
[agent:result]             missed interval on recovery. If False (default), only create the most recent.
[agent:result]         max_active_runs:
[agent:result]             Upper bound on concurrent executions for this job. Default 1.
[agent:result]         start_time_offset_seconds:
[agent:result]             Controls `HOPS_START_TIME`. Three modes:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             - `None` (default) — use the previous cron fire (last execution time). Adapts
[agent:result]               to any cron naturally.
[agent:result]             - `int` — `HOPS_START_TIME = cron_fire + seconds`. Negative values look
[agent:result]               backwards from the fire; positive look forward.
[agent:result]         end_time_offset_seconds:
[agent:result]             Controls `HOPS_END_TIME`. Three modes:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             - `None` (default) — use the cron fire time (`HOPS_END_TIME = cron_fire`).
[agent:result]             - `int` — `HOPS_END_TIME = cron_fire + seconds`.
[agent:result]         skip_to_date:
[agent:result]             If set, reconciliation skips every missed interval strictly before this date.
[agent:result]         max_catchup_runs:
[agent:result]             Upper bound on missed intervals created during reconciliation (keeps most recent).
[agent:result] 
